@startuml A1-analysis-class-diagram
title UC-ADM-02 – Analysis class diagram (C1 sescam-security)
' Source: PLAN18-11.md §3 (C1 owns User, Role, Permission, AuditEvent),
' UC-ADM-02 spec, UC-ADM-03 spec (audit event content), DECISIONS ADR-008.
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class User {
  - accountStatus : String
}

class Role {
  - name : String
}

class Permission {
  - name : String
}

class AuditEvent {
  - actor : String
  - action : String
  - timestamp : DateTime
  - target : String
  - outcome : String
}

User "0..*" -- "1..*" Role : has assigned >
Role "0..*" -- "1..*" Permission : grants >
AuditEvent "0..*" --> "1" User : actor
AuditEvent "0..*" --> "0..1" User : target

note bottom of User
  Spec: "current role assignments and relevant account status".
  Every user has at least one role: without a role the user would
  have no access at all, and the use case only assigns or changes
  roles (it never leaves a user without one).
  Attribute names are a starting point for the analysis workshop.
end note

note bottom of Role
  A Role is a named set of permissions; a Permission is one
  capability (e.g. to manage roles) that several roles can share.
  Keeping them apart lets permissions be reused and lets a role
  change which capabilities it grants without redefining roles.
  A role grants at least one permission (a role with none grants
  nothing).
end note

note bottom of AuditEvent
  Every successful role change is "attributable and available
  for audit" (UC-ADM-02). Records are never modified or deleted
  (ADR-008). Owned by C1, queried in UC-ADM-03.
end note
@enduml
